ext","value":"Motivation and intuition","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"RWB0n8GjrB"}],"identifier":"motivation-and-intuition","label":"Motivation and intuition","html_id":"motivation-and-intuition","implicit":true,"key":"Vs2XJDjAAe"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A temporary logical AND stores a predicate in a clean helper qubit. It can be\ncheaper to compute that predicate, use it, and erase it by measurement than to\nreverse its non-Clifford circuit. Gidney introduced this route for quantum\naddition ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"DsrangK6mt"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"shor_gidney_addition2018","identifier":"shor_gidney_addition2018","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gidney, 2018","key":"FqN2WDkZMr"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"nJvhmpP6So"}],"key":"thFvzrh1Ie"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"BjlVjA9uMk"}],"key":"Dnl1Ie1VUy"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Measurement does not have to destroy the data coherence. Measuring the helper\nin the X basis adds a known conditional phase to the data; a Clifford CZ\ncorrection removes that phase. The helper’s measured value also tells us\nwhether an X is needed to return it to zero.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"Ze19BrlSkn"}],"key":"Pefh1IPMTe"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Executed ideal-circuit checkpoint","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"fJKu1kBNG9"}],"key":"F1ms3kMCUs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The dedicated module tests passed ","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"HWNhNzO38s"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"109 cases","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"wYLDUFkwum"}],"key":"BPNtUO2aYi"},{"type":"text","value":". The generator executed six\nbounded addition checks and two small order-finding checks, and the companion\nnotebook executed all seven code cells in a genuine Jupyter kernel, including\nits circuit figure. The ","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"HMqqQr7Cqh"},{"type":"link","url":"/OpenQuantumAlgorithms-site/assets/generated/shor/measured-and-validation.json","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"validation summary","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"lZFuyrG4CU"}],"urlSource":"../../assets/generated/shor/measured-and-validation.json","static":true,"protocol":"file","key":"zJguh1aAXn"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrecords exact source and artifact hashes. Larger circuit exports remain\ngeneration-only. No physical estimate, hardware execution or mechanized proof\nis claimed.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"vnFhW7pskU"}],"key":"VpRZfguOWH"}],"key":"S7q11aPBlY"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fundamental construction and complexity","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"qq5gDa88zt"}],"identifier":"fundamental-construction-and-complexity","label":"Fundamental construction and complexity","html_id":"fundamental-construction-and-complexity","implicit":true,"key":"Uay6ZDacgi"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For data controls a,b and a clean helper h, our literal computation is","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"oQLU0fvYnx"}],"key":"s3or3WCIpC"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"H(h), T(h), CX(b,h), Tdg(h), CX(a,h), T(h),\nCX(b,h), Tdg(h), H(h), Sdg(h).","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"M5a91UD6n4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first nine gates are a four-T relative-phase construction. On clean-helper\ninputs its |11,0> branch has phase i; the final Sdg removes that phase, giving\n|a,b,0> → |a,b,a∧b>. No claim is made that this computation is an exact CCX on\ndirty-helper inputs.","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"QDFqzD8EoM"}],"key":"mGZx3jIVkD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copy the predicate into an arbitrary data target with CX(h,target), apply\nH(h), and measure h into m. The two uncorrected data Kraus operators are","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"N1eEi1rqva"}],"key":"XOtiYjnLeQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"[\nK_m=2^{-1/2},CZ(a,b)^m,CCX(a,b,target).\n]","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"bijPg3tUE4"}],"key":"fbFtZPLxSZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applying CZ iff m=1 makes both corrected branches CCX/√2. The data channel is\ntherefore exactly CCX in the ideal gate model, including coherent inputs and\nentanglement with other registers. Applying X(h) iff m=1 clears the measured\nhelper without a second measurement. A separate literal-reset variant is\nprovided for comparison. Each lifetime keeps a and b unchanged until its\ncorrection completes.","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"k7t51jNizj"}],"key":"dUyNkSZMaI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Our ","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"uiljdh0yBf"},{"type":"link","url":"/algorithms/shor/ripple-arithmetic","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ripple baseline","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"xtLUxmFctS"}],"urlSource":"ripple-arithmetic.md","dataUrl":"/algorithms.shor.ripple-arithmetic.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"fgMIa8hzbD"},{"type":"text","value":" has 2w CCX and 4w CX gates before\nlowering. Replacing each CCX gives ","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"crOyczoCPS"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"8w literal T/Tdg gates","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"uDdTXXiLrE"}],"key":"b2Z8iNzdH7"},{"type":"text","value":", compared with\n14w for the standard seven-T decomposition. This is an unoptimized MAJ/UMA\ndrop-in variant, ","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"vnafx8HgRR"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"not Gidney’s separately optimized 4w−4 adder","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"i1X2wyC5YC"}],"key":"o4Snwwt4Ey"},{"type":"text","value":". Measurements,\nhelper storage and controller delays remain costs.","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"lNMy7LXVxX"}],"key":"tBqtKkMuJ3"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Small circuits and important variants","position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"key":"GeFVzUC4uc"}],"identifier":"small-circuits-and-important-variants","label":"Small circuits and important variants","html_id":"small-circuits-and-important-variants","implicit":true,"key":"IZmuMiN9v9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The executed numerical checks cover all eight CCX data basis columns, both\nmeasurement outcomes and coherent data states. They compare the actual\nprimitive circuit’s Kraus operators with an independent classical CCX\npermutation. Addition checks use independent integer arithmetic and coherent\npermutation references. The small default is two-bit addition 3+1 modulo 4,\nwith carry-in zero; the first input and carry must be restored.","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"ynp0BJCHSn"}],"key":"Km5wGaW7vO"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/OpenQuantumAlgorithms-site/assets/generated/shor/measured-and/gadget.svg","alt":"The literal measured CCX replacement: clean helper initialization, four T/Tdg\ngates, helper measurement and the actual conditional phase correction/clear.","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"jKhUZ31MlG","urlSource":"../../assets/generated/shor/measured-and/gadget.svg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"measured-and-gadget