he range, rather than uncounted\nresets. The logical dependency ledger includes a conservative unit-cost\nclassical decision; it is not an optimized physical schedule.","position":{"start":{"line":142,"column":1},"end":{"line":142,"column":1}},"key":"eR0uNK38Lt"}],"key":"Mg1d6RHEpS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":149,"column":1},"end":{"line":152,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ","position":{"start":{"line":149,"column":1},"end":{"line":149,"column":1}},"key":"z70WPvh1SH"},{"type":"link","url":"/OpenQuantumAlgorithms-site/assets/generated/shor/measured-and/scaling.csv","position":{"start":{"line":149,"column":1},"end":{"line":149,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"materialized scaling data","position":{"start":{"line":149,"column":1},"end":{"line":149,"column":1}},"key":"StNvyVvNmV"}],"urlSource":"../../assets/generated/shor/measured-and/scaling.csv","static":true,"protocol":"file","key":"AVFhEgTs3Q"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncontains 16 logical-count rows, comparing both methods at widths\n1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 16, 24 and 31. These rows count constructed circuits; they are\nnot a physical resource sweep or quantum simulations at every width.","position":{"start":{"line":149,"column":1},"end":{"line":149,"column":1}},"key":"KhClI9z6At"}],"key":"ZeUIdBNqrF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":154,"column":1},"end":{"line":158,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For order finding with t clock bits and n integer bits, the existing source\nhas O(t n²+t²) gates and t+3n+4 wires. Replacement adds one helper and O(t n²)\nmeasurements/feedback opportunities. These are source-scaling statements;\nQFT rotation synthesis, repeated quantum trials, classical recovery and\nphysical success require their own full factoring task contract.","position":{"start":{"line":154,"column":1},"end":{"line":154,"column":1}},"key":"VZJsPFyEKY"}],"key":"UEJ3AhPdTG"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":160,"column":1},"end":{"line":160,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fault-tolerant comparison boundary","position":{"start":{"line":160,"column":1},"end":{"line":160,"column":1}},"key":"X1Jk8DNxwX"}],"identifier":"fault-tolerant-comparison-boundary","label":"Fault-tolerant comparison boundary","html_id":"fault-tolerant-comparison-boundary","implicit":true,"key":"VQzLcuT91g"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":162,"column":1},"end":{"line":166,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"No physical estimate has been computed for this instrument. The shared static\nQDK adapter rejects intermediate measurements, resets and if/else. The fixed\ninstrument scheduler also rejects arbitrary source feedback and caps its\ncurrent source width at eight qubits. Neither can be bypassed by silently\ndeleting those operations.","position":{"start":{"line":162,"column":1},"end":{"line":162,"column":1}},"key":"fqyzr4FQ4Y"}],"key":"uSNR5t0AL5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":168,"column":1},"end":{"line":174,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A matched comparison needs an explicit controller/routing envelope, all\ninitializations and readouts, idle exposure, factory transport and fault\nallocations. The old ripple PSSPC table, which assumes logical-zero inputs\nwithout explicit resets, is not the comparator for this prepared instrument.\nThe surface-code assumptions must be frozen equally for a new baseline and\ncandidate. Lower T demand alone does not establish lower time, qubits or\nspacetime volume.","position":{"start":{"line":168,"column":1},"end":{"line":168,"column":1}},"key":"oRSelalNfQ"}],"key":"DfJ9SKyQ5e"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":176,"column":1},"end":{"line":176,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Classical simulation and formalization","position":{"start":{"line":176,"column":1},"end":{"line":176,"column":1}},"key":"tR07oshnkO"}],"identifier":"classical-simulation-and-formalization","label":"Classical simulation and formalization","html_id":"classical-simulation-and-formalization","implicit":true,"key":"wmVNh6RVLm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":178,"column":1},"end":{"line":183,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dense branch-density checks are bounded separately at ten quantum wires and\nan event-by-matrix work ceiling. The larger small order circuits use an\noriginal exact sparse interpreter in Q(ζ16), with ζ16⁸=−1. It applies every\nliteral gate and both measured branches; branches merge only after exact\nequality and helper restoration. It does not substitute a Boolean CCX oracle\nor truncate small amplitudes.","position":{"start":{"line":178,"column":1},"end":{"line":178,"column":1}},"key":"PqV7kPcy4H"}],"key":"qZEWv712oA"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":185,"column":1},"end":{"line":191,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"That interpreter recognizes the intended dyadic π/8 angle model from exact\nPython parameter spellings. It is not an enclosure for binary-angle hardware\nrealization, a general phase simulator or a proof kernel. Numerical density\nchecks and the mathematical derivation are distinct evidence. No Lean or\nRocq proof is integrated for this replacement. The ","position":{"start":{"line":185,"column":1},"end":{"line":185,"column":1}},"key":"vXt3lPFiFu"},{"type":"crossReference","url":"/algorithms/shor","position":{"start":{"line":185,"column":1},"end":{"line":185,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shor formal-reference\nsection","position":{"start":{"line":185,"column":1},"end":{"line":185,"column":1}},"key":"oYvk8QG7b5"}],"urlSource":"../shor.md#available-external-formalization","dataUrl":"/algorithms.shor.json","identifier":"available-external-formalization","label":"available-external-formalization","remote":true,"protocol":"file","kind":"heading","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"available-external-formalization","k